  "about": "Rebuilt from Ace's 21 Street View shots (positions and headings read off their URLs), the Google aerial and the satellite rotated to the building's own axis (u along it, v across it, metres). A cruciform church of terracotta and cream: a long semicircular barrel-vaulted nave with buttress ribs (u -16 to 36), a barrel arm at each of the other three sides of the crossing (SW, NW, SE), each ending in a stepped concentric arch with a stained-glass window; a big maroon ribbed dome on a drum over the crossing; two small maroon domes flanking the front (NE) with a wide stepped pediment, a planted porch deck below it and cobbled rings on the ramps either side; flat aisle roofs with the solar strips; a two-storey terracotta trellis annex with a hedge along each long side (Resort Dr and Portwood St). Heights are estimated from the photographs (nave crown about 17 m, big dome about 26 m).",
